# QA Framework Rules

- Follow existing repository architecture: intent → contract → execution in `src/AgenticQa.Core`, BDD in `tests/AgenticQa.BddTests`, registries in `config/ui` and `config/api`.
- Prefer reuse: search for existing features, step definitions, Page Objects, and registry entries before adding new automation.
- Avoid duplicate helper methods; extend existing support types under `tests/AgenticQa.BddTests/Support/` when needed.
- Maintain separation: Gherkin/features, step bindings, page objects, test data, and assertions stay in their layers.
- Use async/await correctly in Playwright and step definitions; do not block on `.Result` or `.Wait()`.
- Keep assertions readable and deterministic; do not hide failures or weaken assertions to obtain green runs.
- Do not modify production application code to satisfy a test unless the user explicitly authorizes it.
- Make the smallest necessary change; run the smallest relevant `dotnet test` filter after automation changes.
- Artifacts live under `artifacts/` (results, failure-analysis, screenshots, agent-runs); reference paths in triage output.
- Test IDs follow `TC-<AREA>-<NNN>` when creating new intent-backed cases.
